---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Privacy Policy - Glen Lambe Coaching" description="Privacy Policy for Glen Lambe Coaching. Information on GDPR compliance, data processing, and user rights.">
    <section class="py-5 mt-4">
        <div class="container">
            <div class="row justify-content-center">
                <div class="col-lg-10">
                    <h1 class="fw-bold text-white mb-4">PRIVACY POLICY</h1>
                    <p class="text-muted mb-4"><strong>WWW.GLENLAMBECOACHING.IE</strong></p>

                    <div class="mb-5">
                        <h3 style="color: var(--primary);">I. GENERAL PROVISIONS</h3>
                        <p class="text-muted">This Privacy Policy outlines the rules for processing and protecting personal data of Users accessing the website available at www.glenlambecoaching.ie (hereinafter: the "Website").</p>
                        <p class="text-muted">The document has been prepared in accordance with Article 13(1) and (2) of Regulation (EU) 2016/679 of the European Parliament and of the Council of 27 April 2016 on the protection of natural persons with regard to the processing of personal data and on the free movement of such data, and repealing Directive 95/46/EC (General Data Protection Regulation) "GDPR".</p>
                        <p class="text-muted">The Controller ensures that data is processed in a transparent, secure manner and limited to the absolute minimum necessary.</p>
                    </div>

                    <div class="mb-5">
                        <h3 style="color: var(--primary);">II. DATA CONTROLLER</h3>
                        <p class="text-muted"><strong>Website Owner and Data Controller:</strong> Glen Lambe, operating under the name Glen Lambe Coaching.</p>
                        <p class="text-muted"><strong>Registered Address:</strong> [Insert registration address, e.g., 123 Main Street, Dublin, Ireland]</p>
                        <p class="text-muted"><strong>Company Registration Number (CRO):</strong> [Insert CRO number if applicable, or remove this line]</p>
                        <p class="text-muted"><strong>Contact with the Controller:</strong></p>
                        <ul class="text-muted">
                            <li>Phone: [Insert phone number]</li>
                            <li>Email: info@glenlambecoaching.ie</li>
                        </ul>
                    </div>

                    <div class="mb-5">
                        <h3 style="color: var(--primary);">III. PURPOSES AND LEGAL BASES OF PROCESSING</h3>
                        <p class="text-muted">Personal data is processed for the following purposes:</p>
                        <ul class="text-muted">
                            <li><strong>Service fulfillment and handling inquiries:</strong> Providing information about the coaching program, answering questions, and preparing a customized coaching plan based on voluntary contact (Article 6(1)(b) GDPR – processing necessary for the performance of a contract or in order to take steps prior to entering into a contract).</li>
                            <li><strong>Analytics and statistics (GA4):</strong> Analyzing Website traffic to improve its operation and user experience (basis: voluntary consent of the User – Article 6(1)(a) GDPR).</li>
                            <li><strong>Marketing and social proof:</strong> Displaying client transformations, reviews, and integration with social media platforms like Facebook or Instagram (basis: legitimate interest of the Controller – Article 6(1)(f) GDPR).</li>
                        </ul>
                    </div>

                    <div class="mb-5">
                        <h3 style="color: var(--primary);">IV. DATA MINIMIZATION SCOPE AND PRINCIPLES</h3>
                        <p class="text-muted">Following the Privacy by Design principle, the Website limits the collection of data to the necessary minimum:</p>
                        <ul class="text-muted">
                            <li><strong>Voluntary Data:</strong> Name, phone number, email address, and fitness-related information provided during the application process or customer service communication.</li>
                            <li><strong>Automated Data (GA4):</strong> As part of Google Analytics 4, the Controller has implemented IP address anonymization. This means IP addresses of EU users are removed before data is saved on servers, preventing direct identification of the individual.</li>
                        </ul>
                        <p class="text-muted">Providing contact and application data is voluntary but necessary to process your application and provide coaching services. Failure to provide this data will prevent the Controller from reviewing your application and contacting you.</p>
                    </div>

                    <div class="mb-5">
                        <h3 style="color: var(--primary);">V. COOKIES, LOCAL STORAGE, AND CONSENT MANAGEMENT</h3>
                        <p class="text-muted"><strong>Data storage technologies:</strong> The Website uses cookies and Local Storage (LS) technologies saved on the User's end device.</p>
                        <ul class="text-muted">
                            <li><strong>Cookies:</strong> Small text files sent by a server and saved on the user's side.</li>
                            <li><strong>Local Storage:</strong> A separate part of the browser's memory used to store data locally. Unlike cookies, data in LS is not sent to the server with every request and is stored long-term.</li>
                        </ul>
                        <p class="text-muted"><strong>Purposes of use:</strong> The Controller uses the above technologies for:</p>
                        <ul class="text-muted">
                            <li><strong>Service provision and optimization:</strong> Adapting the content of the Website to User preferences (e.g., proper display on mobile devices).</li>
                            <li><strong>Analytics:</strong> Creating statistics to help understand how Users engage with the Website, enabling its continuous improvement.</li>
                            <li><strong>Session maintenance:</strong> Ensuring the seamless operation of Website features after filling out forms (e.g., the application form).</li>
                        </ul>
                        <p class="text-muted"><strong>Third-party partners and services:</strong> The Controller uses web components and scripts of partners who may place their own cookies on the User's device. List of partners/services:</p>
                        <ul class="text-muted">
                            <li>Google Analytics / Google Tag Manager: Traffic statistics and behavior analytics.</li>
                            <li>Facebook / Instagram: Social functions and analytics.</li>
                            <li>Google Forms: Processing and securely managing coaching applications.</li>
                        </ul>
                        <p class="text-muted"><em>Note: The Controller does not have direct control over the privacy policies of third parties. We encourage you to verify the policies of these providers.</em></p>
                        <p class="text-muted"><strong>Consent Management:</strong> You can change your cookie preferences at any time using the dedicated consent banner on our Website or directly in your browser settings. Restricting the use of cookies or Local Storage may affect some functionalities available on the Website.</p>
                    </div>

                    <div class="mb-5">
                        <h3 style="color: var(--primary);">VI. USER RIGHTS</h3>
                        <p class="text-muted">Every User has the right to:</p>
                        <ul class="text-muted">
                            <li>Access their data and receive a copy of it.</li>
                            <li>Rectify, erase ("right to be forgotten"), or restrict processing.</li>
                            <li>Withdraw consent for cookies or marketing at any time.</li>
                            <li>Object to the processing of data.</li>
                            <li>Data portability (receiving personal data from the controller in a structured, commonly used, and machine-readable format).</li>
                            <li>Lodge a complaint with the Data Protection Commission (DPC) in Ireland if they believe data processing violates GDPR.</li>
                        </ul>
                    </div>

                    <div class="mb-5">
                        <h3 style="color: var(--primary);">VII. DATA RETENTION PERIOD</h3>
                        <p class="text-muted">In accordance with the storage limitation principle, personal data will be processed only for the period necessary to achieve the purposes for which it was collected:</p>
                        <ul class="text-muted">
                            <li><strong>Inquiries and coaching applications:</strong> Data processed for the purpose of answering questions or reviewing applications will be kept for the duration of the correspondence, and after its completion for a period of 6 months to maintain continuity of communication, unless a coaching agreement is concluded.</li>
                            <li><strong>Service provision and contracts:</strong> Data necessary to perform the coaching service will be stored for the duration of the service, and subsequently for the time required by law (e.g., tax/accounting documentation) and until the statute of limitations for potential civil law claims expires.</li>
                            <li><strong>Analytics data (GA4):</strong> Data collected automatically is stored for a period of up to 14 months.</li>
                            <li><strong>Marketing consents:</strong> Data processed on the basis of consent will be kept until the User withdraws it.</li>
                        </ul>
                    </div>

                    <div class="mb-5">
                        <h3 style="color: var(--primary);">VIII. DATA RECIPIENTS AND TRANSFERS OUTSIDE THE EEA</h3>
                        <p class="text-muted">Data may be transferred to trusted entities: hosting providers, IT support, and payment processors. In connection with the use of Google tools (GA4, Google Forms) and Facebook/Meta, data may be transferred outside the European European Area (EEA).</p>
                        <p class="text-muted">The Controller informs that:</p>
                        <ul class="text-muted">
                            <li>A Data Processing Amendment has been concluded with Google Ireland Ltd.</li>
                            <li>The transfer takes place on the basis of EU Standard Contractual Clauses.</li>
                        </ul>
                    </div>

                    <div class="mb-5">
                        <h3 style="color: var(--primary);">IX. FINAL PROVISIONS</h3>
                        <ul class="text-muted">
                            <li>The Controller reserves the right to update this Policy.</li>
                            <li>Materials on the Website (client transformations, logos, videos) are protected by copyright and the right to image. Unauthorized copying or distribution is prohibited.</li>
                            <li>This policy enters into force on the date of publication.</li>
                        </ul>
                        <p class="text-muted mt-3"><strong>Last updated:</strong> 17.11.2026</p>
                    </div>

                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>
</BaseLayout>